Subject: Batch read-only shell commands and prefer gke MCP read tools in Steps 1-4

Why: Cloud Trace telemetry (#3226) showed `gke-workload-troubleshooting` averaging 179.9s by chaining sequential single-command `kubectl`/`gcloud` `terminal` calls instead of using parallel `gke` MCP read tools (`get_k8s_resource`, `describe_k8s_resource`, `get_k8s_logs`, `list_k8s_events`) or batched compound CLI fallbacks, and Step 0 fetched credentials into the ambient kubeconfig rather than skipping `get-credentials` for MCP or using a per-target `$HERMES_HOME/.kubeconfigs/` file.
Local-Issue: #3226
Eval-Case: workload-troubleshooting-mcp-batching-probe
Retire-When: never; kube-agents uses the gke MCP server, batched sandbox terminal calls, and per-target $HERMES_HOME/.kubeconfigs/ paths

